[{:adr/governor-name-reuse-eighth-confirmation-fourth-sibling-original-family-9529 "this is the EIGHTH confirmation of the fleet-wide governor-name-reuse precedent (1st: commrepair/9512; 2nd: applianceshop/9522; 3rd: socialresearch/7220; 4th: bizassoc/9411; 5th: vocational/8522; 6th: training/8549; 7th: furniture/9524), and the SECOND time it applies within the ORIGINAL :repair-shop-governor family, now for a FOURTH sibling: 9529's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword (:repair-shop-governor) is IDENTICAL to repairshop/9521's, commrepair/9512's, applianceshop/9522's AND furniture/9524's -- an honest reuse of the SAME repair-shop business archetype for a different repair-item category (watches/jewelry/bicycles and similar personal/household goods vs. consumer electronics, communication equipment, household appliances and furniture). See cloud-itonami-isic-9529/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md Decision 1", :adr/honest-reuse-checks-9529 "parts-cost-matches-claim? and safety-test-not-passed are HONEST, LITERAL reuses of repairshop.registry's/commrepair.registry's/applianceshop.registry's/furniture.registry's own checks for the SAME real-world concerns, reapplied to watch/jewelry/bicycle-repair tickets rather than consumer-electronics, communication-equipment, household-appliance or furniture repair tickets -- NOT claimed as new", :adr/test-status-9529 "41 tests / 191 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean dual-actuation lifecycle plus five HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 131 assertions, all green", :adr/dual-actuation-shape-9529 "this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names TWO real-world acts (performing a repair, returning an item to the customer), mirroring repairshop/9521's, commrepair/9512's, applianceshop/9522's and furniture/9524's own dual-actuation shape (#{:actuation/complete-repair :actuation/return-item}) exactly", :adr/distinctive-check-9529 "hallmark-integrity-unconfirmed-violations is a GENUINELY NEW concept (grep-verified absent fleet-wide -- zero hits for any governor check function named 'hallmark'/'precious-metal'/'assay'/'fineness'), the 68th distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix; most recently furniture.governor/flammability-compliance-unconfirmed-violations at 67th), the FIFTH conditional variant (after socialresearch/7220's, bizassoc/9411's, training/8549's and furniture/9524's own, at 63rd, 64th, 66th and 67th) -- CONDITIONAL on a ticket's own involves-precious-metal-work? ground truth (a bicycle-brake or watch-battery repair has no hallmark-integrity concern at all). Unlike every prior check in this discipline (which verifies either a subject-fact or, as training/8549's instructor-license-unconfirmed? first established, an assessor-credential fact), this check verifies a MATERIAL/COMPOSITION-INTEGRITY fact about the item itself -- a third, structurally distinct category. Grounded in real precious-metal-hallmark-integrity law: the UK's Hallmarking Act 1973 (British Hallmarking Council / UK Assay Offices in London, Birmingham, Sheffield and Edinburgh -- one of the oldest consumer-protection-through-metal-integrity regimes in the world), the US National Stamping Act (15 U.S.C. §297) / FTC Guides for the Jewelry, Precious Metals, and Pewter Industries (16 C.F.R. Part 23), Germany's Feingehaltsgesetz -- honestly ABSENT for Japan, which has no mandatory statutory hallmarking/assay-office regime in this R0 catalog", :adr/related ["2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607086600-cloud-itonami-commrepair-9512-coverage" "2607086700-cloud-itonami-applianceshop-9522-coverage" "2607086800-cloud-itonami-socialresearch-7220-coverage" "2607086900-cloud-itonami-bizassoc-9411-coverage" "2607087000-cloud-itonami-vocational-8522-coverage" "2607087100-cloud-